 - Anything from `/demo`. Judge mode stores nothing.
 - Raw data from OneAquaHealth's closed systems. We only fetch their public sandbox.
 
+## Rain lookups
+
+The dry pipe question is asked only after dry weather, so the API looks up recent rain at the
+spot. It sends Open-Meteo (api.open-meteo.com) the position rounded to 2 decimal places, about
+1 km, even when the person placed a precise pin, and nothing else from the visit. The request
+comes from our API, not from the phone, so Open-Meteo sees our server and the time of the
+request, never the person's address. Weather data by Open-Meteo.com, CC BY 4.0, credited on
+every screen that shows a figure worked out from it.
+
 ## What the hosts log on their own
 
 We do not control the hosting providers' own logs. Plainly:
